{*
	The functions Latte 2.11 registers, plus the two nette/application adds when
	a presenter is attached. They are written like PHP calls, and none of them
	may be underlined.

	group(), hasBlock() and hasTemplate() arrived in the Latte 3 line and are in
	latte-3-only.latte.

	A plain PHP function called from a template is at the bottom: Latte passes
	through anything it does not register itself, so the plugin must not report
	an unknown name here either - a project can register its own.
*}
{var $items = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]}
{var $text = 'alpha'}
{var $position = 4}

{clamp($position, 1, 3)}
{divisibleBy($position, 2)}
{even($position)}
{odd($position)}
{first($items)}
{last($items)}
{first($text)}
{slice($items, 1, 2)|implode:', '}

<p n:if="even($position)">The condition is a function call.</p>
<p n:if="divisibleBy($position, 2) && !odd($position)">Two of them.</p>
<ul>
	<li n:foreach="slice($items, 0, 3) as $item">{$item}</li>
</ul>

{* nette/application, present only while a presenter is attached *}
<a href="#" n:class="isLinkCurrent('Article:detail') ? current">Current link</a>
<p n:if="isModuleCurrent('Admin')">Inside the module.</p>

{* Plain PHP, and a project's own function the plugin cannot enumerate *}
{count($items)}
{strtoupper($text)}
{number_format(1234.5, 2)}
{implode(', ', $items)}
